    "summary": "Description by C H Read on catalogue slip in 1895:\r\nThree lei-hulus, or feather ornaments for the head or neck. One is composed of alternate scarlet and pale green; it is thinner than the average. The second is red with yellow bands at regular intervals, the yellow feathers being left long. The third is plain red.\r\n\r\n(Modern description)\r\nThree head or neck ornaments, lei, made of feathers and vegetable fibre cord.",
